# Line endings are decided here rather than by each developer's git config. This repository is
# written on Windows and built on Linux CI (CLAUDE.md § Working conventions), and a file that
# arrives with the wrong endings fails a lint rule on one machine and passes on the other.
* text=auto

# Binary. Never line-ending converted — a CRLF substitution inside a JPEG or a TTF corrupts the
# file — and never diffed as text, which would print megabytes of noise into a review.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary

# Fonts are binary for the same reason, and the reason matters more here: a font this
# repository ships is served byte-for-byte to every visitor.
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary

# SVG is deliberately absent from the list above. It is text, and keeping it diffable is how a
# change to the club's logo shows up in a review as something a person can read.
